
● I now have deep canonical grounding — 50+ Voidborn ship lore entries plus the
  station network. Here's what the source material actually tells us, before we
  pick directions to render.
     
  What the canon says about the Voidborn

  Their ships aren't built — they're grown. The starter Threshold is "cultivated
  in Nexus Prime's orbital growth bays" over a period called "gestation"; the
  Apotheosis dreadnought matures over months and is "possibly alive." Hulls are
  "crystalline-organic composite," self-repairing, with collection membranes
  engineers call "disturbingly pulmonary." Ships anticipate pilot intent, have
  opinions about destinations, run "warmer during towing, as though the effort is
  metabolic," and prefer "familiar rock." → A species that cultivates biology
  rather than manufacturing it.

  They are a distributed consciousness — "The Collective." The Core (Nexus Prime)
  is literally "the central consciousness of the Voidborn." Synchrony Hub
  "coordinates the alignment of distributed consciousness... exists purely for
  thought." The Nodes are a computational network with failover ("if Nexus Prime
  goes dark, Node Alpha assumes coordination within three ticks"). Drones "share
  consciousness with the ship"; the Consensus/Overmind make a fleet "move as one
  mind — whose mind is unclear." → A networked hive-mind, individuals as partial
  expressions of one whole.

  They distinguish themselves from "organic visitors." Every station notes
  organics are "accommodated / permitted but monitored." A citizen is a
  "fabricator of custom exo-chassis." → They are synthetic or post-organic — 
  bodies are swappable shells, not flesh.

  They treat dimensions/probability/phase as native physics. Pocket dimensions,
  dimensional fractures, "null matter," phase-shifting, probability-field
  navigation, "constructive impossibility," mild temporal déjà vu listed under
  features. The air "tastes of ozone and mathematics." → Beings partly outside 
  normal spacetime.

  Their whole naming language is philosophy + epistemology: Apeiron, Qualia,
  Noumenon, Solipsism, Aporia, Eigenstate, Hysteresis, Plenum. They deliver
  "philosophical texts to study circles." Failures are blamed on "insufficient
  philosophical preparation." And they're cold — cabins "always three degrees too
  cold," "thermal sympathy" — patient, watchful, quiet.

  The existing KB portrait styling already pins individuals as "ethereal, pale, 
  high-collared, ascetic."

  Synthesis: a post-biological, networked collective intelligence that grows its
  technology like tissue, wears swappable crystalline-organic bodies, and lives
  half-anchored in adjacent dimensions. Humanoid in silhouette, wrong in the
  details. That's our raw material.

