  the H3/abstract effects — keeping the two that work (chromatic-split,
  crossfade-drift) and replacing fold-churn + noise-dissolve with something much
  more ambitious: subject-preserving animation, 4D-rotation-driven warps for the
  abstracts, Stargate-style star-streak "probability fields," and a body-shaped
  disintegration. That's real creative design work, so let me brainstorm it
  properly before touching code.



  - abstract_phase_c already is the Stargate look frozen: a bright primary curve,
  self-similar smaller curves behind it, radial star texture. Your vision is
  essentially animating the streaking that the still implies.
  - abstract_fold_a is a nested-pentagon tunnel — a natural fit for a true
  rotating-polytope feel.
  - h3_phase_fold has a clearly separable bright figure against a dark void with
