  Here's how I've decomposed your feedback into work:
  1. Subject-preserving warp — body stays solid, only the surrounding "math"
  geometry moves (for h3_phase_fold's hex ring). 
  2. 4D / rotating-tesseract warp — for the abstract folds (fold tunnel, starred
  folds).
  3. Hyperspace star-streak "probability field" — Stargate-style, fixed curve +
  self-similar secondary curves, stars warping toward/away (for
  abstract_phase_c).
  4. Body disintegration — masked "poof to dust" with wind drift (for
  h3_phase_dissolve).

  Chromatic-split and crossfade-drift stay as-is.

  First and biggest question — the 4D effect. Applying "actual higher-dimensional
