● Excellent — that gives me a clear picture. Let me also lock two smaller
  decisions myself (flag if you disagree): the disintegration loops by ping-pong
  (body intact → fully dusted at the midpoint → reformed), which both loops
  seamlessly and reads as "phasing out of existence and back" — very Voidborn;
  and subject-masking becomes a reusable modifier rather than a one-off, so the
  body-preserving behavior can apply to the warp cleanly.

  Here's the design.

  Design: H3 / abstract animation effects v2

  Shared helper: subject_mask(img, params)
  
  Produces a soft 0–1 body mask. Auto: luminance threshold (bright figure vs dark
  void) → keep largest connected blob → morphological close → Gaussian feather.
  Override: if <src>.mask.png exists beside the keyframe, load it instead.
  Params: mask_threshold, mask_feather. Used by hyper-warp (protect mode) and
  disintegrate.

  New effect: hyper-warp (4D-rotation displacement)

  Normalize (x,y)→[-1,1], embed each pixel into a 4D point (the extra z,w coords
  seeded from radius so there's real structure in the hidden dims), apply a
  genuine 4D rotation through the xw / yw / zw planes (the rotations with no 3D
  analog) by θ(t)=2π·t·turns, perspective-project 4D→2D, and use the resulting
  offset as a displacement field to remap the keyframe. Integer turns (default 1)
  ⇒ full rotation ⇒ seamless loop. Param protect_subject: true composites the
  feathered un-warped body back on top (for h3_phase_fold's figure; the hex glass
  tumbles in 4D while the body stays solid). Params: amp, turns, w_dist,
  protect_subject.

  New effect: hyperspace-streak (Stargate probability field)

  Keep the keyframe's bright curve(s) fixed (detected as bright ridge pixels).
  Build a flow field pointing toward/away from the nearest curve pixel. Streak by
  accumulating the image sampled along the flow with a decaying motion-blur
  trail (streak_len). Add boosted synthetic stars (seeded points near the curve)
  advected along the flow so the streaks read stronger than the faint painted
  texture. Loop: star parametric positions advance by t mod 1 ⇒ continuous
  streaming that returns at t=1. Params: streak_len, n_stars, toward (bool),
  curve_threshold, seed. (This is the effect most likely to need a visual
  iteration pass after first render — like noise-dissolve did.)

  New effect: disintegrate (body dust)

  subject_mask → for masked pixels, advect outward along a wind vector +
  turbulence, fading with distance; a per-pixel noise threshold vs alpha(t)
  drives the dissolve front so the body erodes into drifting dust and reforms.
  Background untouched. Ping-pong alpha=0.5(1-cos(2πt)) ⇒ intact→dust→intact,
  seamless. Params: wind_angle, wind_px, turbulence, grain, seed.

  Wiring (anims.json) & keeping old effects

  - h3_phase_fold, h3_v_fold2, h3_v_fold3 → hyper-warp protect_subject:true
  - abstract_fold_a (+ add abstract_fold_b) → hyper-warp full
  - abstract_phase_c → hyperspace-streak
  - h3_phase_dissolve → disintegrate
  - chromatic-split & crossfade clips unchanged.
  - Old fold-churn / noise-dissolve stay in the registry (tested, still valid
  generic tools) but are no longer referenced by default.

  Future enhancements (noted, not built)

  - 4D approach (2) synthetic projected-polytope wireframe overlay, and (3)
  hybrid warp+overlay.

  Testing

  Per effect: loop-seamlessness (t=0 vs t=1 within tolerance), shape/dtype, and
  behavior checks (mask non-empty on a synthetic bright blob; disintegrate
  midpoint differs from endpoints; streak elongates a point source; hyper-warp
  identity at t=0). Plus a smoke render through render().

