  A few specifics worth your eye:
  - hyper-warp hidden dimensions — I seed the 4th (w) and 3rd (z) coords from
  each pixel's radius so the 4D rotation actually does something non-trivial (a
  constant w would make it a boring scale). This is the choice that determines
  what the "tesseract tumble" actually looks like; it's the most likely knob to
  revisit after first render. 
  - hyperspace-streak honesty — I flagged it as the effect most likely to need a
  visual tuning pass (streak length, star count, flow quality), same as
  noise-dissolve did. The loop invariant is still unit-tested.
  - Mask override path — I chose foo.png.mask.png (sits next to the keyframe).
  Easy to change if you'd prefer foo.mask.png.
  - abstract_fold_b — I added it as a new clip; if that keyframe doesn't exist at
  plan time, that row gets dropped.




