● The keyframe itself already shows dust on the right side — useful context. Now
  let me compute the mask and sample the dissolve progression, and I'll fold in
  your second note about hyperspace-streak too.
     
  disintegrate — the subject mask is full of holes that follow the facial
  features. The mask (luminance threshold + largest component) catches the bright
  rim/hair/halo but drops the mid-tone face interior — eye socket, cheek shadow,
  jawline, lips fall below threshold → feature-shaped holes. So only the
  rim/hair dissolves and the face stays "solid" (it was never masked). At t=0.5
  (alpha=1.0, supposed full dissolve) the face is still completely intact. That's
  the root cause of "only part of the head" and "catching on cheekbones/eye
  sockets/jawline." The fix is mask hole-filling, plus making the dust fully
  clear at peak and revealing background instead of black.

  hyperspace-streak — noted: streaks too faint/slow; need brighter and faster
  toward the curve.


● I now have the full picture for this refinement round — three asks on
  disintegrate (fill the mask holes so the whole figure dissolves; complete the
  fade-out + a few frames longer; reveal background not black) and four on
  hyperspace-streak (brighter, faster toward the curve, match the keyframe's
  existing thin radial star-streaks, and more of them). That last image (#5) is
  the original abstract_phase_c — I can see the fine long radial streaks in the
  corners that the synthetic ones should emulate.



● I have everything for this refinement (now "v3"). Since you want both
  background treatments, disintegrate needs an alpha-capable path. Here's the
  design.
     
  Design: animation effects v3 — disintegrate completion + alpha, hyperspace 
  polish

  1. subject_mask — fill holes (root fix)

  Add _fill_holes (pure-numpy flood-fill of background from the image border on
  the inverted mask; anything unreached is an interior hole → set to foreground).
  Apply after largest-component, before feather. The figure becomes a solid 
  filled silhouette — eye sockets, cheek shadows, jawline, lips included — so the
  whole figure dissolves uniformly instead of catching on features. Also
  benefits hyper-warp protect.

  2. _inpaint_background(img, mask) — the void behind her

  Diffusion inpaint (iterative blur-and-reinsert-known-background) fills the
  masked region with a plausible continuation of the surrounding void/stars.
  t-independent → cached.

  3. disintegrate — rewritten dissolve model

  Per pixel, an advected presence/alpha A:
  - presence = clip((noise + band − alpha)/band, 0,1) · mask, with noise
  normalized to [0, 1−band] so at the peak everything reaches A=0 (fully gone) —
  fixes "only part dissolves / never completes."
  - Dust drifts: A and dust color are inverse-remapped along the wind by an
  offset that grows as each pixel dissolves.
  - mp4 path: out = inpainted_bg·(1−A) + dust·A → dissolves into the revealed
  void (not black).
  - alpha path: the same A becomes the alpha channel.
  - Ping-pong loop (vanish → reform); duration bumped 5s→7s for a slower,
  complete fade.


  4. Alpha output (the "both")

  - New encode_webm_alpha (VP9 yuva420p via the bundled ffmpeg) writing RGBA
  frames; PNG-sequence fallback if VP9-alpha is unavailable.
  - anims.json items gain optional "alpha": true; render/run_batch then also emit
  <file>.webm (transparent where dissolved) beside the .mp4. Gallery keeps
  showing the mp4.

  5. hyperspace-streak — brighter, faster, more, matched

  - Brighter: screen-blend the stars and lift intensity/whiten color.
  - Faster: new speed (travel) multiplier; stars cross more distance per loop.
  - More: default n_stars up (~300→700).
  - Match keyframe streaks: draw long, thin radial streaks (like the corner
  streaks in abstract_phase_c), with brightness ramping up as they approach the 
  curve so the "arrival" reads.

  6. Wiring & tests

  - anims.json: disintegrate clip → duration 7 + alpha:true; hyperspace clip →
  brighter/faster/more params.
  - Tests: _fill_holes closes an interior hole; mask coverage rises after fill;
  disintegrate fully clears at peak (A≈0, body region ≈ inpainted bg) and
  reforms; background pixels untouched; alpha-webm (or PNG seq) is produced;
  hyperspace brighter (higher mean over a dark base) and stars present.
  Loop-seamless throughout.

  This is one coherent v3 spec. Sound good before I write it up?









